'''Aragonese Baliscans''' ([[Aragonese language|Aragonese]] and {{langx|bl|aragoneses}}, {{langx|ca|aragonesos}}) refers to [[Baliscans|Baliscan]] citizens of full or partial [[W:Aragonese people|Aragonese]] ancestry or those born in the [[W:Autonomous communities of Spain|historical region]] of [[W:Aragon|Aragon]] in inland northeastern [[W:Spain|Spain]] who reside in [[Balisca]]. Aragonese Baliscans form one of the largest [[European Baliscans|European ancestry]] groups in the confederation. Between 1857 and 1936, 261,020 Aragonese people immigrated to Balisca, predominately settling in [[Bayara]]. 

Baliscans of Aragonese descent make up a substantial proportion of the Baliscan population, and have historically played an integral role in the socioeconomic development of the [[Baliscan archipelago]].

